    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529-a2">

                <pb facs="0730" n="636" xml:id="pg636"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 1 to inclosure 1 in No.
                        517.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commandant to Mr.
                            Hyatt.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Commandancy of Marine and Captaincy of the Port of Santiago de
                                Cuba</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Cuba</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1896-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic">April 9,
                                1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To the Consul of the United
                        States:</hi></p>
                <p>This day has been conducted to this port by the torpedo boat <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Galicia</hi> the citizen of your nation named Bert
                    Skiller, who, in union with two Germans and an Englishman, was detained by said
                    torpedo boat in a small craft, without a clearance, 3 miles from La Caleta. The
                    said individual has been put in jail, subject to trial by this court, to obtain
                    knowledge of the cause that gave motive to the arrival on these shores; which I
                    hasten to notify your honor for your knowledge.</p>
                <p>God guard you many years,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Manuel de Eliza.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
